WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.410
JOE: Life events and transitions
indicate change, and as we have discussed

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.170
previously, change is often very difficult
for individuals on the autism spectrum.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.820
An individual with autism needs to
be prepared for any changes caused

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.629
by life events and transitions making
the process easier for them to handle.

00:00:18.959 --> 00:00:22.450
BETH: The planning process to prepare
an individual with autism, for a life

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.769
event or transition, should cover
every aspect of that change and how

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:30.670
it will impact the individual, making
the process easier to deal with.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.319
Also, the needs of everyone involved
and those supporting the individual

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:39.670
must be considered, considering how
they are impacted by the life event

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.540
and the emotional needs of all affected
by the change in the situation.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.620
JOE: Seeking the support of others
especially professionals can help to

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:51.869
support everyone concerned and they can
become a good asset to have on board

00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:53.669
when in the process of transition.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.890
BETH: A psychotherapist or counsellor
or another trusted professional such

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.510
as a social worker may be able to offer
guidance and support and a range of

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.560
strategies that may help with change
associated with a specific life event or

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.879
transition that may impact the family.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.780
JOE: Support groups and online
communities may also be a good source

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.350
of help offering their own experiences
and guidance, giving insights into how

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:20.060
to approach the transition process.

00:01:20.429 --> 00:01:24.190
BETH: Informal support networks
can also be helpful directly and

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:27.920
indirectly helping with more general
support that might be needed.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:32.250
Families should not be afraid of seeking
help when they need it to make the

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:35.830
changes associated with life events
and transitions progress more smoothly.

